# Line endings for the files where CRLF actually breaks something.
#
# Deliberately narrow. A blanket `* text=auto` would renormalise the whole repository in
# one commit, which buries real changes; these three are the cases where a Windows clone
# would otherwise produce something that does not run.

# A shell script checked out with CRLF fails inside the container as
# "/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter" — the shebang is read with the carriage return attached.
# docker-entrypoint.sh is the one that matters: it seeds the music and SFX volumes before
# the server starts, so a broken one takes the container down at launch.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Both are read by the Docker daemon rather than by Windows tooling.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf
